			<div class="content" id="post-content-4848983">
									

<p>This is giving me a lot of Class of '76 vibes (I'd suggest checking out more of those articles), but this isn't the clearest idea to read. The elevator pitch is supposed to be the short snappy blurb to get people interested, but it is bigger than the central narrative where you're supposed to explain the story you want to tell here. Maybe focus on the MTF that gets trapped in the book is my suggestion?</p>
<p>I'd suggest rewriting the concept a bit to make it more concise, It's an interesting concept but it needs refining.</p>

