<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article + Tale</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Emotional</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong> Containment, Description, Exploration and Tale connected to it.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> Mansion in which pianist remains is placed 2 miles East in Allegheny National Forest. Anomalous pianist creates world and story of it's fall in his music. People that will hear his music hallucinate through it's whole story being able to hear and see everything, but not being able to interact with that world. People under influence will feel like the story continues for hours while in normal time it's only about 5 minutes long. After seeing it's whole story, influenced individuals show symptoms of extreme depression and inability to die of old age as they are &quot;already dead inside&quot;.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Everything occurs in mansion build 2 miles East in Allegheny National Forest. Previously mentioned anomalous pianist plays a song with length of 4 minutes and 56 seconds, but for influenced person it's like hours. Pianist shows them all tragedies of &quot;lost world&quot;. Everyone who sees the story became extremely depressed and unable to talk about it to the point where influenced individuals commit suicide. People influenced by this SCP are empty. They are alive, but they barely eat, drink or sleep and a they do is look nowhere. People that saw the story are unable to die of old age as they are &quot;already dead inside&quot;. Only one D-Class individual was able to keep part of his sanity and as ex writer, he was able to write just a portion of what he saw as a tale. D-Class few weeks after dies by stabbing his own throat with pen, he was given to write the rest of story.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> I waned to focus on emotional pressure on reader and I just waned to write what and how I feel.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong><br />
I didn't wrote what the story contains for purpose to keep it hidden for now.</p>

