<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Cope&nbsp;Crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Let's do this&#8230;</p>
<blockquote>
<p>A storm that appears once every 4 years in a completely random location on Earth. The rain is red and feels like blood and if touched with bare skin it will turn you into a mindless zombie with increased speed and strength. It is not possible to convert people back to normal.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>So why is it random? Why does it make people turn into zombies? Why do the zombies have increased speed and strength? It's not possible to convert people back to normal? So even SCP-500 can't heal them? I have so many questions.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>This SCP is usually the size of the state of Texas. It will appear on a random day after 4 years in a random location at a random time which makes it much harder to tell if the storm is abroad. The first hour of the storm will appear as just cloudy but after the hour is over, the rain will begin to pour. During the first hour, civilians in the range of the storm will be warned of the storm via EAS on television, radio, and cell phone. Anyone not taking cover will be detained by arriving MTF agents. Aggression towards MTF agents will be met with lethal force. The storm will usually last between 16 to 28 hours and once its over, all civilians in the area must be given amnestics to forget about the past hours of the storm. Anyone lost during the event must be given a cover story as to why they are gone.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What's the narrative? It sounds like you only gave me the containment procedures.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>During the most recent event, a man created a journal explaining his experience of the storm and everything that happens while the MTF guard the streets to keep people safe.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Okay, so I believe this is the narrative. Mind going into a bit more detail?</p>
<p>Overall Thoughts: You barely went into description of the Narrative. All I know is the SCP containment procedures and that a man writing down his experiences with the Foundation and said SCP. I suggest you give the narrative much more detail and thought. I also feel that the anomaly itself makes very little sense. Why zombies? Why blood? Why do the zombies have enhanced psychical abilities? I feel like more thought needs to be put into this stuff. It sounds like you put a bunch of words into a blender and hoped for the best.</p>
<p>You can contact a butterfly to help you out or go to the IRC to get another reviewer. Both have a ton of experience.</p>
</div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Close</a></div>
</div>
</div>

